//? Title: Johnson's all-pairs paths: make negative edges usable
//? Subtitle: Actual potential relaxations, reweighted edges and lazy-heap work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Johnson's algorithm finds directed all-pairs shortest distances when negative
edges are allowed but negative cycles are absent. A single potential calculation
makes every edge nonnegative; repeated Dijkstra searches then restore
original-weight distances. We retain the original three-edge example, expose
actual native operations, exercise cycles and stale heap entries, and measure
how edge order changes preparation work. Checked arithmetic and record limits
make numerical and storage boundaries explicit.
)

\toc

> Begin with the original negative edge

The original graph has edges 0 to 1 of weight 1, 1 to 2 of weight −2, and 0 to 2
of weight 4. Its indirect path costs −1. All potentials start at zero, as though
a synthetic source reached every vertex by a zero-weight edge. The potential at
vertex 2 becomes −2, making the negative edge's reduced weight zero. The native
diagram reads that actual reweight event; its arrows describe the calculation,
not additional graph edges.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/johnson_reweight.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::algorithms::johnson_trace(3, dm::algorithms::johnson_demo_edges());
    std::print("| pass | edge | target before | candidate | target after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        if (e.action == dm::algorithms::JohnsonAction::Potential)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.pass, e.edge, e.before,
                       e.candidate, e.after);
    std::print("\n| edge | u | v | original weight | h u | h v | reduced weight |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.edges.size(); ++i) {
        const auto[u, v, w] = t.edges[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, u, v, w,
                   t.analysis.potentials[u], t.analysis.potentials[v],
                   t.analysis.reduced_weights[i]);
    }
    std::print("\n| source | d to 0 | d to 1 | d to 2 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
        const auto &r = t.analysis.result.distance[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, r[0], r[1], r[2]);
    }
    if (t.analysis.result.distance[0][2] != -1)
        throw std::runtime_error("original answer");
    dm::algorithms::johnson_reweight_diagram(t, 1).save_svg(
        "build/johnson_reweight.svg");
}
```
