> Why changing edge weights preserves the answer

In exact arithmetic, terminal shortest-path potentials satisfy h(v) ≤
h(u)+w(u,v). Consequently

$$
w'(u,v)=w(u,v)+h(u)-h(v)\geq0.
$$
\alttext(The reduced edge weight adds the origin potential and subtracts the target potential, producing a nonnegative value.)

For a path from s to t, intermediate potentials cancel:

$$
w'(P)=w(P)+h(s)-h(t),\qquad d(s,t)=d'(s,t)-h(s)+h(t).
$$
\alttext(All paths between fixed endpoints change by the same endpoint-potential difference; subtract that difference to restore a distance.)

Thus paths with the same endpoints retain their relative weights. Adding a fixed
constant to every edge would instead penalize paths according to their edge
count. Zero reduced weights are valid; the algorithm requires nonnegative edges.
Cycles retain their total weight. A negative cycle makes shortest distances
unbounded below for affected reachable pairs, and this global all-pairs API
rejects the entire problem.

The implementation uses input-order, in-place Bellman–Ford relaxations, stopping
after an unchanged pass or reporting a decrease on pass n. Initial zero labels
make cycles in disconnected components visible. Once reduced weights are
available, each source uses a min-heap ordered by distance and vertex id. Every
strict improvement inserts a new entry; older entries are discarded when popped
if their key differs from the current label. Histories come from that execution,
with no repeated-prefix replay.

> Watch obsolete heap entries leave the queue

The following five-vertex control gives vertex 1 an expensive direct route
before discovering a cheaper route through vertex 2. It also includes a negative
edge and a positive-total cycle. We print the full distance matrix and every
source-zero heap pop. The figure compares the actual reduced labels recorded
immediately before restoration with the returned original-weight row; these
finite values are not separately recomputed searches. Infinity in the matrix
means unreachable.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/johnson_heap.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge> edges = {{0, 1, 10},
                                                             {0, 2, 1},
                                                             {2, 1, 1},
                                                             {1, 3, -2},
                                                             {2, 3, 5},
                                                             {3, 4, 2},
                                                             {0, 4, 20},
                                                             {4, 1, 1}};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::johnson_trace(5, edges);
    std::print("| source | to 0 | to 1 | to 2 | to 3 | to 4 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
        const auto &r = t.analysis.result.distance[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, r[0], r[1], r[2],
                   r[3], r[4]);
    }
    std::print("\n| actual event | popped vertex | popped key | current label | stale |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, reduced, restored;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.events.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.events[i];
        if (e.source == 0 && e.action == dm::algorithms::JohnsonAction::Pop)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, e.u, e.candidate,
                       e.before, e.stale);
        if (e.source == 0 && e.action == dm::algorithms::JohnsonAction::Restore) {
            x.push_back(e.v);
            reduced.push_back(e.before);
            restored.push_back(t.analysis.result.distance[0][e.v]);
        }
    }
    const auto &w = t.analysis.work;
    std::print("\n| BF checks | Dijkstra checks | pushes | pops | stale pops | restored cells |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               w.potential_checks, w.dijkstra_checks, w.heap_pushes,
               w.heap_pops, w.stale_pops, w.restored_cells);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, reduced, "reduced", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, reduced, "",
                                                           {37, 99, 235}, 5).line(x, restored, "original", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, restored, "", {220, 38, 38}, 3).title("Source zero: recorded labels and restored costs").x_label("target vertex").y_label("distance").y_limits(-.3, 3).save_svg("build/johnson_heap.svg");
}
